{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe light in The Hague is fading as I write. I take the coach to Breda tonight, though I confess the journey seems less a necessity than a whim for fresh air. The Dutch spirit is orderly, but I find myself craving the warmth of our home and the sound of the children’s voices.\n\nI must tell you of a strange sight I passed today. A tomb monument, they say by Michelangelo. Alabaster figures of a count and his wife lie upon a black slab, yet above them stand four giants—Caesar, Hannibal, Regulus—holding up the stone. It struck me as a terrible image of history: the dead held aloft by the weight of past empires, while the living are reduced to mere stone. It made me think of how our own freedom is not a gift from nature, but a struggle carried on by the spirits of ages.\n\nI miss you terribly. The wind is rising, and I feel the need for your steadying presence.\n\nYour devoted,\nG."}}],"created":1795080230,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":217,"prompt_tokens":943,"total_tokens":1160,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-DETt4FA6EfwPgWT04dZiF7OV14ykWTke","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":943,"prompt_ms":917.195,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9726352067868506,"prompt_per_second":1028.134693276784,"predicted_n":217,"predicted_ms":5249.472,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.30311111111111,"predicted_per_second":41.14699535496141}}